analysis-v2/

# v1 track artifacts (refactored 2026-05-23)
# Mirror v3 behavior: track briefs + diaries on iteration branches (small text
# files); reports-v1 parquets blocked (large binaries). Strict-trunk discipline
# is enforced at MERGE-time via cherry-pick of src commits only — NOT via
# gitignore (which would break the iteration branch workflow).
reports-v1/**/*.parquet

# Parquet artifacts inside reports-v3/ (e.g., trial_oof_returns.parquet)
# can exceed GitHub's 100MB limit. Keep CSV/JSON reports tracked; never
# commit parquet files into reports-v3 again. Other parquet locations
# (data/features_v3/, etc.) already covered by the data/ rule above.
reports-v3/**/*.parquet

# Top-40 canonical team reruns are reproducible local artifacts. Keep the small common BTC
# benchmark under version control, but not per-team Parquet/CSV output directories.
reports-top40/team-*/

# CUP-20. Everything under reports-cup20/ is a derived organiser artifact, and several of the
# derived artifacts are computed over BOTH sides of the 2024-08-01 cutoff -- the acquisition's
# common BTC report is a daily return and regime-label series running to the sealed window's last
# day, which would hand a team the holdout's realised drawdown and its day-by-day regime sequence.
# Unlike the top-40 track, none of it is a team input: teams read data/cup20/is/ and nothing else.
# Regenerable from the acquisition snapshot by scripts/cup20_build_snapshot.py.
reports-cup20/
# Organiser-only CUP-20 surfaces: the full-universe pure-crypto audit and the organiser's own
# universe summary both describe the sealed side's composition by name. Hash-bound by the
# activation record and held on disk exactly like data/cup20/sealed/, never committed.
tournament/cup20/private/

# Notebook outputs and checkpoints
notebooks/output/
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Claude settings (track commands/skills/agents, ignore the rest)
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
